\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A coefficient pair at every depth}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Block means of a hierarchical precision multiply each
coefficient by #{p} and place it one depth coarser. In
\ref{fdip-009A} the geometric choice has top coefficient #{m},
and multiplication of the class mean by #{\sqrt{p\lambda}}
produces top coefficient #{m/\lambda}. Can a different top
coefficient make one pair #{(\lambda,m)} describe every depth,
and what sum over the #{p} finer residues goes with that choice?}
